.TH TX\-BROADCAST 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
tx\-broadcast \- tx\-broadcast (HOST\-SIDE, network): send ONE already\-signed transaction, after the human reads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tx\-broadcast \-\-chain btc|ltc|doge|eth [\-\-url URL] < signed tx  (asks for a code on the terminal)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
its summary on the terminal and types a code. Irreversible.
.nf
.RS 2
  tx\-broadcast \-\-chain btc|ltc|doge|eth [\-\-url URL] < tx\-sign output (or signed hex)
.RE
.fi
UTXO chains: POST {esplora}/tx; EVM: eth_sendRawTransaction. The id the server returns must
equal the id computed locally, or status is "error". Defaults as utxo\-fetch.
.SH WARNING
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
.br
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
.br
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
.br
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, recipes/README.md
